    "media:imagetext": "+ WELCOME ABOARD\nPre-meal beverage and snack as requested\nSALAD\nFresh Asian salad\nwith napa cabbage, red cabbage, carrots, mango\nwith sesame ginger dressing\nENTRÉE\nSeared beef short rib\nwith hoisin barbecue sauce, jasmine rice, broccolini and carrots\nPan seared salmon\nwith coconut red curry sauce, Thai coconut risotto,\nstir-fried bell pepper, carrots and onions\nVegetarian chili and polenta cake\nwith ripened tomatoes, kidney beans, bell peppers, onion,\nchipotle peppers and soy crumble\nEXPRESS DINING\nIf you'd prefer a consolidated meal service, please ask your flight\nattendant for our express dining service. You can choose to receive all\ncourses at one time or only select items and your meal will be presented\nat your request.\nDESSERT\nIce cream sundae\nVanilla ice cream with chocolate fudge\nand brownie crumble topping\nEgg custard tart\nAssorted cheese plate with crackers\nGouda, Grand Cru Gruyère, Butterkäse, grapes and crackers\n+ MID-FLIGHT SNACK\nSelection of sweet and savory snacks\n+ BEFORE ARRIVAL\nMonterey Jack and red pepper egg white bites\nwith fire-roasted pepper sauce, charred tomato,\nroasted fingerling potatoes and chicken apple sausage\nHorchata steel-cut oatmeal\nwith agave apple\nVegetarian Option\nWe apologize if your preferred menu option is not available on today's\nflight. Menu items are subject to substitution.\n260C001\nUSA to Japan: Lunch/Dinner (LD81)\n11/22\nUNITED\n+\nPOLARIS.\nLooking for\nadditional comfort?\nOn scheduled flights\n12 hours or longer,\nsleep amenities, such as\nfleece-lined slippers and\npajamas, are available to\nhelp you relax and catch\nsome ZZZS.\nAsk your flight attendant\nfor availability.",
